I'm now incorporating `replace` into all `Navigate` components to clean up the navigation history and avoid unexpected back button behavior, as suggested. I'm also removing any traces of the `UpdatePassword` component and its imports, as I aim to follow instructions as strictly as possible. The `user` prop should be passed to the dashboard and admin components. The default route will use the dashboard or login path based on user state.


**Debugging Environment Interactions**

The error message, "No routes matched location...", remains crucial. I suspect the environment might be passing an incorrect `location` object, specifically a full URL, to the router. The `HashRouter` is designed to work with the hash portion only. I'm going to investigate if there's any modification to `window.location` that could be causing this issue. I am also investigating whether some conflicting routing logic exists, particularly in this hosted environment.


